[{:seon.task/name "web-server-threads-are-joined-at-stop"
  :seon.task/plan "When the web proc binds its port, ring-chez-adapter's :fibers strategy runs its acceptor and its connection sweeper as two futures (two OS threads of Jolt's agent pool, clojure-agent-pool; the adapter's `start-sweeper!` and its acceptors in src/ring_chez/adapter.clj). The acceptor polls accept() in accept-poll-ms slices; the sweeper is (Thread/sleep 100) in a loop, a clock (AGENTS §4). stop-server waits for the acceptor but only flags the sweeper, so after `seon.root/stop!` the sweeper outlives its owner for up to 100 ms: root's thread count after stop! depends on timing, so bin/check lifecycle runs with SEON_WEB_PORT=0. The adapter's :keep-alive-timeout-ms 600000 and :write-timeout-ms 60000 (`seon.web/web-proc`) are application timers and literals (docs/clocks.md#time-decides-owed-its-owners-fix). Correct: the listener is a fiber parked on the listen fd's readiness (jolt.io-poller); an idle connection parks on its own read (a fact, not a sweep); a stuck write is the peer's half-open socket, the kernel's keepalive (the owner's exception); the web proc's ::flow/stop returns after both are gone. Then `seon.root/declared-threads` drops its \"clojure-agent-pool\" 2 for a listening web proc, and lifecycle runs with the web on. Deletes: start-sweeper!, the accept poll slice, the two adapter timeouts, the SEON_WEB_PORT=0 in bin/check's lifecycle step. A dependency change: on a jolt/<topic> branch of the adapter."
  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/proofs #{seon.root-test/root-threads-are-what-root-declares}}
 {:seon.task/name "call-checks-the-origin"
  :seon.task/plan "What exists: `POST /call` (the handler in `seon.web`, `seon.web/requests`) submits forms to one or every live agent and calls root's functions, and it reads no Origin or Sec-Fetch-Site header. Any page open in the owner's browser can POST to 127.0.0.1:<port>/call. v1 refused cross-origin on every POST (::same-origin middleware, ~/src/seon/src/seon/render/route.clj). Correct: refuse (403, recorded) a POST whose Origin is present and not the dashboard's own origin, or whose Sec-Fetch-Site is cross-site; one row in docs/failure-points.md."
  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/proofs #{seon.web-test/a-cross-origin-call-is-refused}}]
